+# Postman / Bruno Import Guide
+
+## Import the Collection
+
+1. Make sure the server is running: php artisan serve --port=8000
+2. Open Postman or Bruno
+3. Click Import
+4. Use URL: http://localhost:8000/docs/api.json
+5. All endpoints are imported automatically
+
+## Set Up Environments
+
+Create two environments:
+
+### Local
+- base_url: http://localhost:8000/api/v1
+- api_key: abouelsid-secret-key-change-in-production
+- auth_token: (empty — fill after login)
+
+### Production
+- base_url: https://api.abouelsid.com/api/v1
+- api_key: (production key from .env)
+- auth_token: (empty — fill after login)
+
+## How to Get a Token
+
+POST {{base_url}}/auth/login
+Body: { "email": "admin@abouelsid.com", "password": "password" }
+Copy the token from the response and paste it into auth_token variable.
+
+## Authentication
+
+Public endpoints: add header X-API-Key: {{api_key}}
+Admin endpoints: add header Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}
+All endpoints: add header Accept-Language: ar (or en)
+
+## Quick Test Sequence
+
+1. GET  {{base_url}}/dishes          → should return 5 dishes
+2. GET  {{base_url}}/branches         → should return 2 branches
+3. GET  {{base_url}}/testimonials     → should return 10 testimonials
+4. GET  {{base_url}}/timeline         → should return 5 items
+5. POST {{base_url}}/auth/login       → get your token
+6. GET  {{base_url}}/catering/quote-requests  → requires token
